## 3. What this repository does not contain

- No third-party skill, plugin, binary, or CLI archive is vendored or
  redistributed. Framework-shipped capabilities are the project's own; every
  tool choice is operator-installed and operator-local.
- No operator-private data: no credentials, tokens, auth state, machine-specific
  paths, vault contents, or tracker identifiers. The upstream cleanliness guard
  (`scripts/check-clean.{sh,ps1}`) exists precisely to keep those out of a
  publicly cloneable tree, and AOS inherits that rule.

